From eb5f63ea2a9954291a26ba232972d1eca06cb3f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "John (PinKushin)" <pinkushin1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:26:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] perf: step and build particle effects on worker threads,
 byte-identical

Bursts now run in UpdateNewEffects' three passes (particlemgr.cpp:1841-1884):
a serial pass in offer order does every read and write of the collection and
asks every caller callback (Model, DormantAt, History; a rebuild's replay runs
here too); the played steps run one effect per worker from answers asked
serially; then every write lands in offer order, so _bursts is mutated in the
serial sequence and enumerates in the serial order. A key offered twice
flushes first. Build decides what is drawn serially, gathers each effect into
its own slot on the workers, and appends the slots in order (our addition:
the engine threads simulation only).

cl_frame_workers (ours; default ProcessorCount/2 capped at 8; 1 is serial)
reaches ParticleEffects.Workers through ViewFrame.

Tests: ParticleEffectsWorkersTests compares 46 frames' batch bytes, census
and counters serial vs 2 and 8 workers, backwards and interleaved schedules.
Sabotage: merging gathers in completion order, and committing inside the
worker, each reddened the backwards and interleaved tests; removing in the
serial pass reddened the seek-order test. Each restored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
